    "faq": {
      "type": "section-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is a pre-shampoo treatment?",
            "content": "<p>A pre-shampoo treatment is applied to wet hair in the shower, before you shampoo and condition.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does it work for all hair types and types of damage?",
            "content": "<p>Yes! No.3PLUS works on all hair types, textures, and for all types of damage, such as heat, styling, environment, mechanical friction, color and chemicals, and hard water.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is there protein or keratin in No.3PLUS?",
            "content": "<p>No, it is free of protein and keratin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_TTW6Kf": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need to use No.0 Intensive Bond Building Treatment with No.3PLUS Complete Repair Treatment?",
            "content": "<p>No, you don't need to use No.0 Intensive Bond Building Treatment with No.3PLUS. No.0 was designed to be used alongside the original No.3 Hair Perfector for an extra boost. However, No.3PLUS is a next-generation formula and already delivers that enhanced performance on its own—so No.0 is not required.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_TCicgF": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does No.3PLUS Complete Repair Treatment replace No.3 Hair Perfector?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. No.3PLUS is replacing the original No.3 Hair Perfector. It's the next-generation version of No.3, with an upgraded formula that delivers everything you loved about the original with even better results. Like No.3, it's a pre-shampoo treatment, but it only needs 3 minutes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_UKTCRx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between No.3 and No.3PLUS?",
            "content": "<p>While the original No.3 focused primarily on internal bond repair, the new No.3PLUS formula features an upgraded, next-generation formula that provides complete repair and protection. No.3PLUS repairs both the inside and outside of the hair strand (360° cuticle-to-cortex repair), adds protection to help prevent future damage, works in just 3 minutes (compared to 3-10 minutes for No.3), and is formulated for all hair types.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_zDJJVJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I use No.3PLUS Complete Repair Treatment, and how often should I use it?",
            "content": "<p>Apply a generous amount to wet, unwashed hair from mid-lengths to ends. Leave it on for 3 minutes, then rinse, shampoo, and condition as usual. Use it 1–3 times per week (or every 1–3 washes), depending on your hair's level of damage.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
